## Example Usage

Restart, password reset, resize and parameter-group application return an API error with HTTP 409 `restore_not_activated` until a database restored into a new database activates successfully, including when the restore failed. No password, plan or configuration change starts on refusal; wait for successful activation before applying those changes. Applying or clearing a parameter group is excluded from declarative OpenTofu coverage because this resource has no parameter-group field; the shared client method remains available to explicit callers, and MCP supports the action.

Manual full/incremental backups are imperative operations and remain excluded from declarative OpenTofu resources. The shared API client's backup methods send requests once. Both types refuse with 409 `backup_in_progress` while a backup is pending/in_progress, `database_busy` for nonterminal work on the actual source VM, or a pending restore/recovery/PITR reopen guard. An unavailable incremental never silently falls back to full. Transport errors, node 5xx/408/429 and invalid acknowledgements can retain pending backup/task ownership: inspect database backups/tasks before retrying. A caught dispatch failure may answer user API HTTP 200 `success: false` (admin HTTP 400); the client still returns an error. Acceptance is not completion.

